      "message": "If I\u0027m reading this correctly: currentRatio/thresholdRatio here are value.current/value.total and tConfig.value/100 from HealthMetric::checkThreshold() (health_metric.cpp:161-162), i.e. 0..1 fractions. But UNITS is hardcoded to MetricUnit::Percent, and elsewhere in this file Percent is treated as a 0..100 range (see the CPU metric\u0027s ValueIntf::minValue(0.0)/maxValue(100.0) in initProperties(), health_metric.cpp:89-91).\n\nShould ReadingValue/ThresholdValue be multiplied by 100 here to match the declared Percent unit?\n\nAs written, a metric crossing at e.g. 12.75% would report ReadingValue\u003d0.1275 with Units\u003dPercent in the resulting entry.",
